# Build-context hygiene for repo-ROOT Docker builds.
#
# The code-exec sandbox image (deploy/docker/deepagents-sandbox.Dockerfile) builds with
# `context: .`, so without this file `docker compose up --build` ships the ENTIRE working
# tree (~85GB: an 84GB data/ tree, .venv, .git, node_modules, scratch datasets) to the
# Docker daemon before the build can start. Keep ONLY what the root-context Dockerfiles
# actually COPY (the RareSpot assets + third_party/yolov5 + the runtime sources).
#
# Per-service builds with their own context (control-plane -> backend/controlplane,
# worker/image-service -> backend/deepagents_runtime, frontend -> frontend) are NOT
# affected by this file — they have their own .dockerignore where needed.

# Version control & CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Python envs / byte-compiled / tool caches
.venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# Node / frontend artifacts (frontend is never a root-context build input)
**/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Local scratch, logs, planning, docs, editor cruft
.tmp
**/.tmp
*.log
.DS_Store
planning
docs
.claude
legacy
output
test-prairie

# Large local/scratch datasets that are not build inputs
*.ome.zarr
**/*.ome.zarr

# Local secrets / env files (never bake into an image)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The runtime data tree is ~84GB and never a build input — EXCEPT the RareSpot
# weights the sandbox image bakes in (deepagents-sandbox.Dockerfile COPYs
# data/models/yolo/RareSpotWeights.pt). Exclude data/* contents, re-include models.
data/*
!data/models
